{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <algorithm>\\n#include <cstdint>\\n#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n\\n#if defined(__ARM_NEON) || defined(__aarch64__)\\n#include <arm_neon.h>\\n#endif\\n\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nstatic constexpr uint32_t MOD = 1000000007u;\\n\\n#if defined(__ARM_NEON) || defined(__aarch64__)\\nstatic inline uint32x4_t add_mod(uint32x4_t a, uint32x4_t b) {\\n    const uint32x4_t sum = vaddq_u32(a, b);\\n    // Both inputs are below MOD. Unsigned subtraction wraps precisely\\n    // when sum < MOD, making the unsubtracted sum the smaller value.\\n    return vminq_u32(sum, vsubq_u32(sum, vdupq_n_u32(MOD)));\\n}\\n#endif\\n\\n// An obstacle immediately preceding this interval resets the left carry\\n// to zero. Values initially hold contributions from the preceding row.\\nstatic inline void scan_interval(uint32_t* dp, int begin, int end) {\\n    uint32_t carry = 0;\\n    int j = begin;\\n#if defined(__ARM_NEON) || defined(__aarch64__)\\n    const uint32x4_t zero = vdupq_n_u32(0);\\n    for (; j + 4 <= end; j += 4) {\\n        uint32x4_t values = vld1q_u32(dp + j);\\n        values = add_mod(values, vextq_u32(zero, values, 3));\\n        values = add_mod(values, vextq_u32(zero, values, 2));\\n        values = add_mod(values, vdupq_n_u32(carry));\\n        vst1q_u32(dp + j, values);\\n        carry = vgetq_lane_u32(values, 3);\\n    }\\n#endif\\n    for (; j < end; ++j) {\\n        uint32_t sum = dp[j] + carry;\\n        if (sum >= MOD) sum -= MOD;\\n        dp[j] = sum;\\n        carry = sum;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n, m;\\n    cin >> n >> m;\\n    vector<vector<int>> blocked(n);\\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\\n        int i, j;\\n        cin >> i >> j;\\n        blocked[i].push_back(j);\\n    }\\n\\n    vector<uint32_t> dp(n, 0);\\n    dp[0] = 1;\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n        auto& obstacles = blocked[i];\\n        sort(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end());\\n        obstacles.erase(unique(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end()), obstacles.end());\\n\\n        int begin = 0;\\n        for (int column : obstacles) {\\n            scan_interval(dp.data(), begin, column);\\n            dp[column] = 0;\\n            begin = column + 1;\\n        }\\n        scan_interval(dp.data(), begin, n);\\n    }\\n\\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << endl;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Exact four-lane NEON prefix scans over obstacle-free row intervals should shorten the DP dependency chain while eliminating per-cell obstacle checks and row copies.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Retains quadratic grid traversal with O(N+M) storage. Handles duplicate obstacles, blocked endpoints, short intervals, and N=1. Includes a scalar fallback. Not executed or measured.\",\n  \"research\": {\n    \"queries\": [],\n    \"urls\": []\n  },\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Store sorted, deduplicated obstacle columns per row to identify independent scan intervals.\",\n    \"Replace two-row DP and copying with an in-place modular prefix scan.\",\n    \"Use ARM NEON shift-and-add prefix scans with exact unsigned modular reduction and scalar tails.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
